"notes": "Cash basis (modified cash) governmental funds; business-type funds (Water, Sewer, Garbage) are accrual. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds statement Total column (p5); roll-forward 3,458,447 + 2,901,997 - 2,828,242 + 639,626 - 706,306 = 3,465,522. Business-type from the proprietary revenues/expenses statement total column (p7); no single total printed so totals computed; roll-forward 5,770,983 + 403,259 + 66,680 = 6,240,922. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position total column (p1). General Fund: the budgetary comparison schedule (p10, has budget column) is not recorded in detail because the General Fund departments combining schedule (pp14-15) is more detailed; revenue lines use its Total column, expenditures are per department (non-zero cells only; each department column adds to its printed total and all tie to 1,154,403). The p10 General budget schedule totals agree with actuals (resources 1,531,607; charges 1,154,403; transfers out 34,220). Street and LB840 budget schedules and the nonmajor combining statement recorded per fund (ARPA fund has no revenue/expenditure, only transfers out 135,975). The Street schedule's single Debt service line 70,301 is split into principal 49,125 and interest 21,176 using the Street column on p5. The trimmed PDF contains no budget schedules for the Water, Sewer or Garbage funds, so no business-type detail lines exist beyond the basic statements (p6-p9 fund columns not repeated). Proprietary cash flows statement p8-9: Total column on p9. Read pages 1-15 of 15"
